### rustc 1.98.0-nightly (57d06900f 2026-05-27)
### src: p2_three_observation_classes.rs

### compiled clean

### p2. three observation classes over one shipped-shaped carrier pair
### pair: W=13, F=0, unsigned. carrier A = u16 (2 bytes), carrier B = u32 (4 bytes)
### domain: all 8192 declared values; binary arms over all 8192 x 8192 ordered pairs

SIGMA_SIZE  (nullary; supplied by the host language, not by arvo)
  S1         size_of                                        SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  2 vs 4                   as required
  S2         align_of                                       SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  2 vs 4                   as required

SIGMA_BITS  (the encoding: MATLAB bin, IEEE 754 interchange, to_le_bytes)
  B1         encoding stated over the declared width W      agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  C1 ctl     encoding stated over the container             SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  v=0                      as required

SIGMA_VAL   (arithmetic, with the projection back to W after every step)
  V          Add/Wrap, arity 2, projected                   agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  V          Add/Sat, arity 2, projected                    agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  V          Mul/Wrap, arity 2, projected                   agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  V          Mul/Sat, arity 2, projected                    agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  V          Xor/Wrap, arity 2, projected                   agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  V          Xor/Sat, arity 2, projected                    agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  V          chain d=1, Add/Wrap, projected                 agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  V          chain d=4, Add/Wrap, projected                 agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required

SIGMA_VAL   C2a: unprojected AND the intermediate can exceed the narrow carrier
  C2a ctl    Mul/Wrap, arity 2, projection OMITTED          SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  a=9,b=7282               as required
  C2a ctl    Mul/Sat, arity 2, projection OMITTED           SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  a=9,b=7282               as required
  C2a ctl    chain d=8, Add/Wrap, projection OMITTED        SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  x=8,k=8191               as required
  C2a ctl    chain d=16, Add/Wrap, projection OMITTED       SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  x=0,k=4096               as required
  C2a ctl    chain d=8, Add/Sat, projection OMITTED         SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  x=8,k=8191               as required

SIGMA_VAL   C2b: unprojected AND the intermediate cannot exceed it (the region)
  C2b        Add/Wrap, arity 2, projection OMITTED          agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  C2b        Add/Sat, arity 2, projection OMITTED           agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required
  C2b        chain d=4, Add/Wrap, projection OMITTED        agrees     required=agrees     -                        as required

controls: the comparators are not stuck reporting equality
  C3 ctl     encoding at W=13 against W=14                  SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  v=0                      as required
  C3 ctl     Add/Wrap at W=13 against W=14                  SEPARATES  required=SEPARATES  a=1,b=8191               as required

### reading: the carrier separates the pair through SIGMA_SIZE and through
### nothing else. C2 establishes that SIGMA_VAL's blindness is bought by the
### projection rather than given, so it is an obligation on the design and not
### an observation about it.

### exit 0
